[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Scandinavian Defence"]
[Variation "Nf3 Variation"]
[ECO "B01"]
[Character "positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "good-bishop,queenside-castling"]

1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Qxd5 3. Nf3 Nf6 { Develops a piece without allowing the queen to be hit by a knight yet. }
4. d4 ( 4. Nc3 Qa5 { Same retreat square as the main line. } 5. d4 { Transposes to the main line: this is the same position as 3.Nc3 Qa5 4.d4 Nf6 5.Nf3. } 5... c6 )
4... Bg4 { Develops the bishop outside the pawn chain before ...e6 would shut it in. It also pins the knight on f3 to the queen on d1. [%cal Gg4f3] }
5. Be2 Nc6 { Develops and attacks d4. The queen on d5 and the knight on c6 both press on that pawn. [%cal Gc6d4] }
6. Be3 e6 { Opens the bishop on f8 and keeps the centre closed so White has few targets. }
7. Nc3 Qd7 { The queen steps out of the attack and prepares long castling, where the rook will also look at d4. }
8. O-O O-O-O { Castles on the queenside, and the rook on d8 adds to the pressure on d4. }
9. h3?! { This lets Black win a pawn. After the trade on f3, the d4 pawn is defended too few times. } 9... Bxf3 10. Bxf3 Nxd4 { Takes the pawn: the bishop and knight both defended it, but the bishop is gone. } 11. Bxd4 Qxd4 12. Qxd4 Rxd4 *
